<color_light_red>    Disclaimer for Salvaged (WIP):</color>
<color_light_red>******************************************************************************</color>

<color_white>Q: </color><color_yellow>Work In Progress?</color>

<color_white>A: </color><color_light_gray>Salvaged is a work in progress that intends to diverge significantly from its origin.  Updating to a new version of it will most likely make save-games and worlds incompatible.</color>

<color_white>Q: </color><color_yellow>What is the point of the current build?</color>

<color_white>A: </color><color_light_gray>To get off the ground with some significant changes from the fork but overall a stable-enough setup to try out.</color>

<color_white>Q: </color><color_yellow>Are any builds going to be preserved if I want to download an older version?</color>

<color_white>A: </color><color_light_gray>Yes, but not for a while yet. I intend to work my way up to a 1.0 release and save a copy of that as a branch.</color>

<color_white>Q: </color><color_yellow>Does this mean that a build that isn't x.0 is an experimental?</color>

<color_white>A: </color><color_light_gray>No. True experimental builds are their own branch tested privately. Anything released onto github as an x.yz release can be considered "mostly stable", but not as solid as I intend a full x.0 release to be.</color>
